                                                            <h3 id="ala_about_us" class="o_default_snippet_text">
                                                                <span class="o_animated_text o_animate o_anim_zoom_in o_visible o_animated"
                                                                      style="animation-name: o_anim_zoom_in; animation-play-state: running; visibility: visible;">WELCOME TO ST. EUGENE.....</span></h3>
                                                            <p>
                                                                St. Eugene CBSE School is a new English-medium, co-educational school preparing to open its doors for the academic year 2027-28. We are being built around one simple conviction: a good school shapes character just as carefully as it shapes marks.
                                                                <br></br>
                                                                <br></br>
                                                                The campus is being planned from the ground up for the CBSE curriculum - naturally lit classrooms, dedicated science and computer laboratories, a library, and generous open space for sport, music and the arts. Every decision is made with one question in mind: what will help a child learn well and grow up kind?
                                                            </p>
                                                        </div>
                                                    </div>
                                                </div>
                                                <div>
                                                    <p>
                                                        Our founding batch will be admitted to LKG, UKG and Classes I to V. From there the school grows by one class each year until it reaches Class XII, so the first children who join us can complete their entire schooling here.
                                                        <br></br>
                                                        <br></br>
                                                        Joining a founding batch is a rare thing. Class sizes stay small, teachers know every child by name, and the students themselves help set the traditions this school will carry for decades. Admission is open to all children irrespective of caste, creed or community.
                                                    </p>
                                                </div>
<!--                                            </div>-->
                                        </div>
<!--                                    </section>-->
                                </section>
                                </div>
